    dct:description "This is a constructive graph-theoretic existence claim and can be settled by explicit finite-description constructions for arbitrary dimension. No empirical coverage problem remains once the intended notion of equivalence is stated." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For each finite dimension d, encode the integer lattice using vertices with two labeled outgoing edges and a graph construction that represents the required coordinate moves, then exhibit analogous constructions for trees and nested graphs. Verify graph isomorphism to the target structures or identify a degree constraint that makes the construction impossible." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Equivalent to an array depends on whether edges may encode paths rather than immediate neighbors.", "Two outgoing connections may need labels or directed-path gadgets." .
